branch: feature/fact-is-monoid
worktree: ../okay-wt-fact
spec: specs/di.md (module-facts / di-multibind), docs/di.md

why: `Fact[V]` declares `empty` and `combine` under other names —
  that is `Monoid[V]`, which this core has had in Fold.scala all
  along, with instances for Vector, List, String and every
  Alternative. Two names for one thing is exactly what this
  repository forbids, and the cost is paid by every declaration: a
  contributor writes the two methods by hand instead of one line.

what: `Fact[V]` becomes a key that CARRIES its monoid — the common
  declaration is `object Routes extends Fact[Vector[Route]]` and
  nothing else; a custom rule passes its own monoid, which is what
  Needs.Declared needs (its merge dedups). Monoid gains the small
  factory that makes that readable. Facts/installing unchanged in
  meaning.

next: reshape Fact, add Monoid.of, migrate the two users, docs
